                <div class="post-content">
                    <blockquote>Starting from late July to October, Bali would be one of the best spots to encounter reef manta.</blockquote>
                    <p><span class="firstcharacter">I</span>f sharks make you lose your cool, then mantas will play it cool around you and your diving buddies. They could be found in warm temperate and tropical waters. Making them easy to be spotted while basking or floating just around shallow water. </p>
                    <p>Yet, Mantas could swim in a different manner. When travelling over deep water, mantas swim at a constant rate in a straight line, making it one of the most wanted diving experiences. Sometimes you might see them in formation, eating large quantities of zooplankton. It is possible as they do not possess sharp teeth. They sieve food particles out of the water using rows of tiny plates in their mouths.</p>
                    <p>This feeding phenomenon occurs at the perfect time of diving season. Starting from late July to October, Bali would be one of the best spots to encounter reef manta. It would be a good idea to start earlier in June as well since cold water is equal to manta’s best mood generator. When they are in a good mood, you’ll have a good shot ! Breathtaking pictures underwater and unforgettable memories.</p>
                    <p>Mantas are mistaken with stingray most of the time. There are several differences we can take notes here. They do not have a stinger or barb, where stingrays could hurt someone with it. Stingrays usually swim around the ocean bottom. If you encounter this kind of fish in the open ocean, rest assured that it is our friendly manta. Sometimes mantas even jump out of the water to get rid of the parasites around their body.</p>
                    <p>Severe pollution, entanglements and irresponsible gill rakers threaten mantas in the open ocean. Moreover, they have a slow reproductive rate which makes them vulnerable as animals.</p>
                    <p>Seeing the condition of the ocean nowadays, what would you do  to appreciate this majestic creature? Join other divers in marvelous diving experience with manta at these amazing diving spots.</p>
